# Keep the Docker build context small. docker/Dockerfile only COPYs three things:
#   dist/docker/host/  natives/linux-x86_64/  data/cs2-assets-inventory.json
# Everything heavy is excluded here (the committed artifacts alone are multi-GB).
.git/
artifacts/
cache/
walker/
host/
scripts/
docs/
tests/
natives/windows-x86_64/
# Bare-name .so dev symlinks (libprotobuf.so -> libprotobuf.so.33.4.0) are link-time-only. Created
# by WSL on the Windows filesystem, they appear to BuildKit's context loader as symlinks it rejects
# ("invalid file request"). The walker loads the VERSIONED lib (libprotobuf.so.33.4.0) directly via
# $ORIGIN, so these are unneeded at runtime — keep them out of the build context. (Versioned files
# like *.so.33.4.0 do NOT match this and are kept.)
natives/linux-x86_64/*.so
# Exclude the whole dist/ EXCEPT the published host the image consumes.
dist/
!dist/docker/
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
